From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Garcia-Madico Portabella <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:48:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/37] ASoC: codecs: wcn-bt-slim: select channel bit 0 for the
 TX port in the sco parameter

The manual "sco" parameter still enabled the SCO transmit port with bit 1
in its channel select register, the very mistake dai_startup() had already
fixed: the vendor driver writes 1 << port, and the transmit port is port 0.
Writing bit 1 points the port at a channel nothing carries and the capture
comes back as exact digital silence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c
index be0fec7b1..aea884166 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c
@@ -699,9 +699,10 @@ static int wcn_bt_slim_sco_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
 
 	if (on) {
 		ret = wcn_bt_slim_port_enable(wcn_bt, WCN_PGD_PORT_RX_SCO, true, 0);
+		/* bit 0 for the transmit port, as in dai_startup() */
 		if (!ret)
 			ret = wcn_bt_slim_port_enable(wcn_bt, WCN_PGD_PORT_TX_SCO,
-						      false, 1);
+						      false, 0);
 	} else {
 		wcn_bt_slim_port_disable(wcn_bt, WCN_PGD_PORT_RX_SCO, true);
 		ret = wcn_bt_slim_port_disable(wcn_bt, WCN_PGD_PORT_TX_SCO, false);
